;; FOUND by the ESH-0101 guard coverage gate. Ledger: SW-84.
;; WRONG ON EVERY AXIS (jit, aot-o0, aot-o2, vm-src, vm-eskb) — not a
;; divergence, a uniform conformance gap, which is exactly the class no
;; native-vs-VM differential can see.
;;
;; R7RS 6.11: `raise` invokes the current exception handler; "if the handler
;; returns, a secondary exception is raised in the same dynamic environment as
;; the handler." So a handler that returns normally must NOT let the program
;; continue as though nothing was raised.
;;
;; Observed: the enclosing guard never fires and the whole form quietly
;; evaluates to the handler's return value. A raise disappears, exit 0.
;;
;; want: guard-fired
;; got:  ignored
(display
  (guard (g (#t 'guard-fired))
    (with-exception-handler (lambda (e) 'ignored)
                            (lambda () (raise 'esc)))))
(newline)
